in{aligned}r\\cdot (q\\times p) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4((-2)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)-(1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3)-2(1\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =-20+1-14 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2145564f-b143-5694-829e-a9e30f5dc092" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419790}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419789 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419786 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "069decae-ea7d-53a6-9d7f-6cd1604d5e45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419779}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419779} :answer-field/id #uuid "0082553f-6022-5a48-bc6b-791b1c483f07" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "944d3b7e-a470-59f8-92c4-a8abf2a8b72b" :question/math-academy-id "q-317329" :question/problem "Find $b\\cdot (c\\times a)$, if $-5a\\cdot ((6b)\\times (4c))=120.$\n\n$b\\cdot (c\\times a)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5a\\cdot ((6b)\\times (4c)) & =120 \\\\ (-5)\\cdot 6\\cdot 4\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =120 \\\\ (-120)[a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =120 \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c) & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (c\\times a) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "69f520c8-2f68-5cc8-8bb4-1d0fcdb03028"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419790 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419785 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aadbe221-860c-5e54-a0de-bd7fb0bef36e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419781}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419781} :answer-field/id #uuid "cea71914-4f17-5f64-8016-140e481b698d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "20209d26-6af3-5176-8409-17df2aefc0b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-317313" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨1,-3,0⟩$, $b=⟨-2,2,0⟩$ and $c=⟨2,0,-4⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(2\\cdot (-4)-0\\cdot 0)\\,-\\,(-3)\\,((-2)\\cdot (-4)-0\\cdot 2)\\,+\\,0\\,((-2)\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =1\\,(-8)\\,-\\,(-3)\\,(8)\\,+\\,0\\,(-4) \\\\  & =-8+24+0 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7ce27cb2-7851-562f-a805-9613dfe990e5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419791}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419791 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f56b9f8-00ca-5814-abb9-6c5a7caba35e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419780}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419780} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dd14090-bb12-5afc-8250-d9460b7c0f27" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419783}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f15d30b5-fe4a-5207-9935-fd7503715554" :question/math-academy-id "q-317326" :question/problem "Let $a=⟨-2,0,-1⟩$, $b=⟨-3,-1,4⟩$ and $c=⟨5,-2,-2⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\,((-1)(-2)-4\\cdot (-2))\\,-\\,0\\,((-3)\\cdot (-2)-4\\cdot 5)\\,+\\,(-1)\\,((-3)\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =(-2)\\,(10)\\,-\\,0\\,(-14)\\,+\\,(-1)\\,(11) \\\\  & =-20+0-11 \\\\  & =-31.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "85680ae8-e720-54c1-a502-614781ce6410" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419789}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419792 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287975 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "343abe13-b014-58c0-913d-2fc9f7a11d8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285270} {:answer/id #uuid "4c3b1e45-a9c8-5b28-b558-ec4bc793eb4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285496} {:answer/id #uuid "a878dcad-4ddf-585b-a29e-6f1bfa1aa273" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286324} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e6bcc3-f1d7-59c6-953b-c03961aeaf47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286630} {:answer/id #uuid "fbedc400-7438-5567-8dfa-d1cfcb39be79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287087}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287087} :answer-field/id #uuid "42a770db-2d9f-5df9-858e-0db4cb77fe94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ae812812-92a4-5aa7-85f9-50adcd0043cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-20059" :question/problem "Find $c\\cdot (a\\times b)$, if $3a\\cdot (\\sqrt{2}b\\times 3c)=18\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor out the constants and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a\\cdot (\\sqrt{2}b\\times 3c) & =18\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot [a\\cdot (b\\times c)] & =18\\sqrt{2} \\\\ a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $c$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (c\\times b) & =-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $c$ and $a$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c\\cdot (a\\times b) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d94231c6-3192-5dc5-bd63-54e41758bbbe" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419788}}] :activity/title "The Scalar Triple Product" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419778}] [{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134774} :activity/id #uuid "c8768805-6c91-5b41-a3a9-4287350b3afa" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050425 :topic/id #uuid "47bc97de-e4cb-5992-8c54-201c61752e0a" :topic/math-academy-id 2149} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134774 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135091 :tutorial/content "Remember that if $X$ is a binomial random variable in which there are $n$ experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment, then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\binom{n}{x} p^x (1-p)^{n-x}.\n$$\n\nIt can be shown that the expected value, variance, and standard deviation of a binomial random variable $X$ can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\ \\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\ \\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "872af947-d3c7-525f-8bb9-21d55de36921" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4452 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "0b2b3592-e0b4-5a5e-93ad-e27455156dd3" :step/math-academy-id 27404 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134775}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134775 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133845 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133660 :question/id #uuid "da211af4-8acc-56f9-9b5f-8f2d9b026c70" :question/math-academy-id "e-7395"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb06ab09-4bf5-5f87-a6cf-d71c2c9d3296" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050651}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134522} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134523} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421983} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421985} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421987}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Mean of a Binomial Random Variable"} :step/id #uuid "5d083e48-b0c1-507e-980f-a93e7c776da4" :step/math-academy-id 27405 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134776}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134776 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133846 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133661 :question/id #uuid "6f20b6aa-5867-5079-ac47-ba1f3f6486f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-7396"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9e1f419-8442-5192-a1fa-44b5bedeff56" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134524} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134525} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421984} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421986} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421988} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421991} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447208} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447209}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Variance of a Binomial Random Variable"} :step/id #uuid "7e54fa6b-94f6-51ed-b883-5e50fbef31ba" :step/math-academy-id 27406 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134777}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134777 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133847 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133662 :question/id #uuid "c33c8f5f-6640-5d53-8803-8b4cfaccea6a" :question/math-academy-id "e-7397"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c66a7ba5-1019-56bd-b915-bb725ee4a499" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134526} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134527} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421989} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421990} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447205} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447206} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447207}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Standard Deviation of a Binomial Random Variable"} :step/id #uuid "6bc95e77-3f78-52e2-890a-fdf8d97395f3" :step/math-academy-id 27407}] :activity/title "Mean and Variance of the Binomial Distribution" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186134018}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447210} :activity/id #uuid "67edc56b-a9ee-5fab-b142-813c8f1ec3bc" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050425 :topic/id #uuid "47bc97de-e4cb-5992-8c54-201c61752e0a" :topic/math-academy-id 2149} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447210 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447205 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0be445e0-0375-5ea8-9459-c53e6d50f177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447176} {:answer/id #uuid "1584bfe0-d966-5daa-998c-79952fa3b326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3.31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447177} {:answer/id #uuid "2aff8426-f35a-554a-8a66-38d43ce76d6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3.33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447178} {:answer/id #uuid "47c31032-8b56-50f5-af9a-6bf5990b3a5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3.13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447181} {:answer/id #uuid "a7256240-6989-55a6-87d8-09e0234b61e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447193}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447181} :answer-field/id #uuid "74ad51d2-25d4-59e0-a633-9b2e1070afdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447202}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1bcd51a1-0665-5138-a53c-48e05f564d89" :question/math-academy-id "q-84695" :question/problem "A processor manufacturer determines that $2%$ of the processors it produces are defective. A quality control officer inspects a random sample of $500$ processors. What is the standard deviation of the number of defective processors found in the sample? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of defective processors.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=500$ processors\n\n- the probability of a processor being defective is $p=2%=0.02$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(500,0.02).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the standard deviation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{np(1-p)}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the standard deviation of the number of defective processors is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(500)(0.02)(1-0.02)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9.8} \\\\  & =3.13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."} :step/id #uuid "048a1307-200e-5108-a025-827c957dc173" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447214}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447211 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447206 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04c30f5a-bf33-559a-b8a4-5e69bbf5720d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.923" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447175} {:answer/id #uuid "3ff7dee6-d555-52cc-9d52-dea07a26c3b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.732" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447180} {:answer/id #uuid "50c8789a-ed1d-5026-941b-7b2b50d0c177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.702" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447184} {:answer/id #uuid "7b195181-6ca7-5730-8661-e95dd7cb57ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.023" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447189} {:answer/id #uuid "bec1fd83-dfc0-5da0-b29c-9bbb9be7c789" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.903" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447195}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447180} :answer-field/id #uuid "e27dc486-028e-5b85-8121-cb4f3fc8a15b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447204}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "47805108-6203-5bb3-98d1-dea670ffc279" :question/math-academy-id "q-84763" :question/problem "A fair $8$-sided die with numbers $1$ through $8$ is rolled $12$ times. What is the standard deviation of the number of times we get an even number? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times we get an even number.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=12$ rolls of the die\n\n- the probability of getting an even number (i.e., a $2,$ $4,$ $6,$ or $8$) on any roll of the die is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{4}{8}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(12,\\frac{1}{2}).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the standard deviation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{np(1-p)},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the standard deviation of the number of times we get an even number is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (1-\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =1.732\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."} :step/id #uuid "281fc6c5-f0d6-53e7-acdb-64ce6dd2027e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447212}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447212 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447208 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d7bac8f-9400-5b68-a61f-a99ce6b49dd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447179} {:answer/id #uuid "760a9935-e1d0-5e24-b023-e735d9955b4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447188} {:answer/id #uuid "c055988d-f3bd-553d-8e1a-22088530e411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447196} {:answer/id #uuid "cd2d6056-d2b9-56b3-a91d-fd1294acea48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447197} {:answer/id #uuid "e069e05b-9f37-5c93-86b4-5b5e0d856a6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447199}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447197} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cf5258d-4410-5e8c-87c9-4f4a5aa05a93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447201}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "66116800-3925-5364-86bb-866dbabfb7d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-89407" :question/problem "It is known that $40%$ of a given population have blood type O$+.$ What is the variance of the number of people in a random sample of $100$ people having blood type O$+?$" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of people having blood type O$+.$\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=100$ people\n\n- the probability of finding a person with blood type O$+$ is $p=40%=0.4$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(100,0.4).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the variance of the number of people with blood type O$+$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =(100)(0.4)(1-0.4) \\\\  & =(40)(0.6) \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2a403e6a-cb61-53cc-8787-e8ddb2f89be6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447213}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447213 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447209 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5abfb6fc-60ea-572f-ac7e-6a6e6c6c8fc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8.875" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447185} {:answer/id #uuid "695a0aa4-a1fe-5cfe-b2b6-0c3978ac7745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9.355" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447187} {:answer/id #uuid "7eb92730-9656-59a5-a7c5-6a2dcae9c03e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9.375" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447190} {:answer/id #uuid "bc2e1e19-49ff-5edf-a50a-d36611e5e680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8.575" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447194} {:answer/id #uuid "d42c80c4-5881-571e-8e6e-4dd57a871e0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9.575" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447198}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447190} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9ef3f22-a619-5b50-8f97-3dc74dbda9d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447203}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ca0fbb1f-e0c9-5b4f-9fe5-ceb4b1f414a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-130761" :question/problem "A new drug has a $75%$ probability of curing a patient within a week. If $50$ patients are treated, what is the variance of the number of cured patients within a week?" :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be the number of cured patients within a week.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=50$ patients in the sample\n\n- the probability that the new drug cures a patient within a week is $p=75%=0.75$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(50,0.75).$ \n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p),\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\n So, the variance of the number of cured patients within a week is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\  & =(50)(0.75)(1-0.75) \\\\  & =(50)(0.75)(0.25) \\\\  & =9.375.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3e456f34-784c-5b15-be45-6dc17016e9ad"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447214 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447207 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49f3e3ee-5aef-556d-85bb-ab132171fd77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15.77" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447182} {:answer/id #uuid "507f6b15-d100-55b8-b5e7-f81ff6635824" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.557" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447183} {:answer/id #uuid "5cfc7388-da64-5a3f-998a-1a44096afad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.755" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447186} {:answer/id #uuid "92f9993e-cd44-5db5-bae3-94facbcc06d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "17.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447191} {:answer/id #uuid "96b119d8-e7fe-5c56-b4a4-0f900739f445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.775" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447192}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447192} :answer-field/id #uuid "071baea7-b677-5ff5-ad57-c766dc91d228" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5b0b4129-44a0-54cb-bf0f-c1b1c637d428" :question/math-academy-id "q-84696" :question/problem "A fair spinner is designed so that $30%$ of its surface area is painted in red. Tom spins the spinner $15$ times. What is the standard deviation of the number of times the spinner lands on red? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times the spinner lands on red.\n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- there are $n=15$ spins\n\n- the probability of landing on red is $p=30%=0.3$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(15,0.3).$\n\nFor a binomial random variable $X,$ the standard deviation is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[X]}=\\sqrt{np(1-p)}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSo, the standard deviation of the number of times the spinner lands on red is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(15)(0.3)(1-0.3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3.15} \\\\  & =1.775\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."} :step/id #uuid "7b808605-f501-5056-8071-6d7f1c92fb43" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447211}}] :activity/title "Mean and Variance of the Binomial Distribution" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447174}] [{:activity/expected-seconds 1080.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120715} :activity/id #uuid "80511d12-b7f3-5570-8b75-694c2aa3ad46" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050830 :topic/id #uuid "6a093d52-40f2-54b8-8982-db428e58bab5" :topic/math-academy-id 1807} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120715 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186121050 :tutorial/content "If we are given an equation of a plane using the dot product, we can always obtain an equation in terms of $x,$ $y,$ and $z.$ For example, suppose we have the plane that passes through the point $P(-7,5,-2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 3,-6,5 \\rangle.$\n\nFirst, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -7,5,-2 \\rangle,$ and we can write down the equation of the plane using the dot product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-6,5⟩ & =⟨-7,5,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-6,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-6,5⟩ & =-61\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation, we substitute $\\mathbf{r}=\\langle x,y,z \\rangle$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-6,5⟩ & =-61 \\\\ 3x-6y+5z & =-61 \\\\ 3x-6y+5z+61 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis final equation is called the **Cartesian equation of the plane**.\n\n![](images/77/77f18981dda500889655225eabbec730b7b295e6b16cec1700d56c2e27e0ac91.png)\n\nNote that in the equation \n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}3}x+({\\color{blue}-6})y+{\\color{blue}5}z+61 = 0,\n$$\n\nthe coefficients next to $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ are the coordinates of the normal vector \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\langle {\\color{blue}3},{\\color{blue}-6},{\\color{blue}5} \\rangle\n$$\n\n." :tutorial/id #uuid "81332607-6152-5770-b33d-8b80c630fc8d" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3256 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "c247ca81-f4a5-53d1-8429-f69593877343" :step/math-academy-id 17922 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120716}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120716 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119832 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119643 :question/id #uuid "01f32313-178c-5626-91af-110907202416" :question/math-academy-id "e-4936"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b34272b7-a7ad-5a58-974e-54cca957d06e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049436}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120231} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120285} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262860} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262861} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262862} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304823} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304824} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304837} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304929} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314765} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338825} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413736}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Equation of the Plane Perpendicular To a Given Vector"} :step/id #uuid "7a8bd938-5945-5ebb-a062-1d4409d4ccd2" :step/math-academy-id 17923 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120717}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120717 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119833 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119644 :question/id #uuid "d92eb242-104f-55cd-82dc-7620e2f4e636" :question/math-academy-id "e-4937"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2173739c-cd59-58ed-a265-8ee88c982ae0" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048850}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120233} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120237} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262887} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262888} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304928} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311649} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311650} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311651} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311664} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311665} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311697} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311717} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311718} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338826} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363934} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364302} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413735} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419421} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419422} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423157}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Equation of the Plane Perpendicular To a Given Line"} :step/id #uuid "38691512-c8ac-58b3-b639-597249a111ce" :step/math-academy-id 17924 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120718}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120718 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119834 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119645 :question/id #uuid "aa7c3400-9bc0-5f3a-84e5-f3cc2bb87f5d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4938"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "80c443e5-a0b2-5aae-ac8d-27449a8049a3" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120282} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120284} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262889} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262890} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302310} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311666} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311667} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311668} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311669} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311670} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311671} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363024} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387873} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393015} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393022} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423960}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Plane Given Its Cartesian Equation"} :step/id #uuid "4e18819d-30d0-5673-a2f4-2264aa09fbde" :step/math-academy-id 17925 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120719}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120719 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119835 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119646 :question/id #uuid "8a9e1070-0ca0-5f24-ac89-999c9271a91b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4939"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0efe5b11-2c87-58e9-bf7c-e1eecb07adf2" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049132}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120232} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120283} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262901} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302288} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304912} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311692} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311695} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311696} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311708} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314753} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338833} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413737} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419423}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Cartesian Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Vectors"} :step/id #uuid "311c08f2-aa3d-5ea5-8386-44e9771e47c6" :step/math-academy-id 17926}] :activity/title "The Cartesian Equation of a Plane" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186120018}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046659} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419424} :activity/id #uuid "0a7d7d24-69e8-5aec-803a-f5712a252473" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050830 :topic/id #uuid "6a093d52-40f2-54b8-8982-db428e58bab5" :topic/math-academy-id 1807} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419424 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419422 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08c0fd5d-eb30-51ed-9d57-ff0d86d1b905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-y+z-2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419403} {:answer/id #uuid "25dcf144-1a51-5366-9800-5383c00b5a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-2y-z-2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419405} {:answer/id #uuid "2b822cf8-78b8-5c6f-ba5e-a61ce1027e3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-2y-z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419406} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf4ea99-1c7e-5b6b-af27-f81db06966e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-x-2y-z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419410} {:answer/id #uuid "b32a3885-cdf4-51dc-ad0e-0a3c46647043" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-y+z-5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419412}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419405} :answer-field/id #uuid "b30e511f-0a3e-547f-96f1-0bfc53ad4766" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "70aeaa22-2b90-533e-ab1d-9dbd9f885f48" :question/math-academy-id "q-70807" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-1,1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$\\frac{x-2}{-1}=\\frac{y-1}{2}=\\frac{z+1}{1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨1,-1,1⟩.$ From the canonical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨-1,2,1⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨-1,2,1⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,1⟩ & =⟨1,-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,1⟩ & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2,1⟩ & =-2 \\\\ -x+2y+z & =-2 \\\\ -x+2y+z+2 & =0 \\\\ x-2y-z-2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "4426cd88-0ed0-5a8a-bd40-151d1e9d59dd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419428}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419425 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419421 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66b70f6a-e851-54e5-aa28-b6a025e9ece5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "57" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419408}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419408} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f1bb041-bd3b-51ec-95b9-ab27a720aff3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419416} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0061273-aae7-5a50-ba3b-7dbc44ba608c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419411}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419411} :answer-field/id #uuid "51f6537d-feab-5ce3-9fc6-f89624d037a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419418} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "373d6628-e7af-5c99-8ea7-bda3f45e1294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419407}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419407} :answer-field/id #uuid "c79424ce-ee00-57d0-b195-b7db6dde7351" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "53aad395-ec2e-5a47-9cdb-e404625e4482" :question/math-academy-id "q-330576" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(7,4,-3)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$\\frac{x-3}{5}=\\frac{y-2}{4}=\\frac{z+1}{-2}.$\n\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,+4y\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n$z\\,-$\n{{field-3}}\n$=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨7,4,-3⟩.$ From the canonical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨5,4,-2⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨5,4,-2⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ & =⟨7,4,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ & =57\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨5,4,-2⟩ & =57 \\\\ 5x+4y-2z & =57 \\\\ 5x+4y-2z-57 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "62621dfb-b37e-5d44-bdc0-8c2aa74e902d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419426}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419426 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311671 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43ac71e4-1f43-51f8-bfa4-a92855f4700b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309261}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309261} :answer-field/id #uuid "7faaceec-cd8b-568a-858c-271760090279" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "580b7964-a0b4-59ea-bd21-b56d80484ba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309413}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309413} :answer-field/id #uuid "93f3390e-533a-5d25-83c0-c5daa77f3ccf" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311213} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ccc2dae-6d3d-5c97-a2ff-2660720cb731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308836}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308836} :answer-field/id #uuid "95d0ab30-64b1-59c5-b1be-e3cbd8256de2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311226}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "04886b81-54da-502a-b95c-1502eb418ce2" :question/math-academy-id "q-336241" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $12y-6z-30=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$\n\n$(r-⟨0,0,$\n{{field-1}}\n$⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,$\n{{field-2}}\n,\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩=0$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨0,12,-6⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12y-6z-30 & =0 \\\\ -6z & =-12y+30 \\\\ z & =2y-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $y=0$, we get $z=-5.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-5)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,-5⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,-5⟩)\\cdot ⟨0,12,-6⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6908c1c1-4988-5f64-8e7b-f1732fcb1a7f"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419427 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "102de1fa-9039-5418-a721-6fc419237fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+5y+8z+9=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419404} {:answer/id #uuid "90536ec6-2590-5af2-a702-9be2e4b1ecdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+8y+5z+6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419409} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f81252-3be5-5daa-a718-63070020d187" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x-5y+8z+7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419413} {:answer/id #uuid "c8ca9437-ca61-5c50-96e0-f167dfcd51fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+5y-8z+11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419414} {:answer/id #uuid "d6eccb3f-c3a2-58a8-b47e-683c853ab3af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+5y+9z+15=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419415}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419404} :answer-field/id #uuid "34e50549-8287-5dd0-82ee-b77b6017695a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419417}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "e08b1f6c-36a3-5d41-8737-49d26e8563c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-128459" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(1,-2,0)$, $P(3,-4,1)$ and $Q(2,1,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vectors of the points $A,P$ and $Q$ are $a=⟨1,-2,0⟩,\\,p=⟨3,-4,1⟩,$ and $q=⟨2,1,-2⟩.$\n\nFirst, using the $3$ points we build $2$ vectors parallel to the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1} & =\\overset{\\to }{AP} \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,1⟩-⟨1,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,1⟩ \\\\ {v}_{2} & =\\overset{\\to }{AQ} \\\\  & =⟨2,1,-2⟩-⟨1,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,3,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+5j+8k \\\\  & =⟨1,5,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,5,8⟩ & =⟨3,-4,1⟩\\cdot ⟨1,5,8⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,5,8⟩ & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,5,8⟩ & =-9 \\\\ x+5y+8z & =-9 \\\\ x+5y+8z+9 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6d308039-35f2-59e5-b262-324c1a8c2bf2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419425}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419428 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262889 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f87268c-9742-5090-b7cb-521a5d8bbe66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,1⟩)\\cdot ⟨2,4,-4⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260021} {:answer/id #uuid "a390ff13-0937-5eb3-b38b-3df5883b8889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,-2⟩)\\cdot ⟨-4,4,-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261300} {:answer/id #uuid "def43d7d-583f-5acb-a4e0-a37562571a5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,-2,4⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261844} {:answer/id #uuid "f4c13bd5-c05b-5f70-93b5-0ba177da222f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262013} {:answer/id #uuid "ffcc7a65-376c-57d0-ac3e-a501019e18ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,2⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262119}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262013} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b80e560-2ad7-58b7-9b2c-28eb67acbc7c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262329}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0f6aca53-4308-58bc-afcc-f2738d69d1e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-128380" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $4x+4y-2z=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨4,4,-2⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+4y-2z & =0 \\\\ 2z & =4x+4y \\\\ z & =2x+2y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=0.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,0)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨4,4,-2⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "c018d688-d281-50de-9674-51b7847b124c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419427}}] :activity/title "The Cartesian Equation of a Plane" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419402}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423962} :activity/id #uuid "2e339301-4273-5fe3-adcf-f9263b991a91" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050830 :topic/id #uuid "6a093d52-40f2-54b8-8982-db428e58bab5" :topic/math-academy-id 1807} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423961 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338833 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10191765-520e-51b1-b616-6aed299a1951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x+3y=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336181} {:answer/id #uuid "7daf1c63-6468-51ad-b441-f7fb571f725e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-3z+4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337169} {:answer/id #uuid "ba9bfc06-e53d-546a-8e5c-41d1b1999a5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3x-2y-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337685} {:answer/id #uuid "c52efad2-ab20-5349-b4af-05ecdf7d704d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337785} {:answer/id #uuid "f09bbdc2-0929-5b68-b7a0-f2e4bd00ad0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x+3y-4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338137}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338137} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f92cb71-8832-51de-ba25-618de4d73dc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338468}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ee138f11-2a9e-5208-a49a-f5a947f6c08b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70833" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,0,-3)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=⟨-3,2,0⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨0,0,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of the point $P$ is $p=⟨2,0,-3⟩.$\n\nNow, we need to find the normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & ={v}_{1}\\times {v}_{2} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =2i+3j \\\\  & =⟨2,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,3,0⟩ & =⟨2,0,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,0⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,3,0⟩ & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,0⟩ & =4 \\\\ 2x+3y & =4 \\\\ 2x+3y-4 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "24b7f863-ce6a-5264-b6ec-ac8e65ecdb05"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423962 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120233 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0395970e-0d9a-5762-bb5c-e46f2d38b8c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-y-5z+11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423949} {:answer/id #uuid "4b65c837-ece2-5b2d-a1d6-63cd8cc028b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+3y-7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423953} {:answer/id #uuid "5e5c8545-4573-5ed8-bdbb-b47cb8a05b58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x+3y-1=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423954} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e87eac-968b-5331-95b6-4aa94e8c328b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2y+z+7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423956} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a52ec1-f084-5a8c-880c-5ed843166cc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2x-y-5z+7=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423958}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423958} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc839475-9e1b-518e-9233-6715536351ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e3a2e450-d136-5240-a920-568065ef68bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-33146" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(0,2,1)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n$\\frac{x-1}{-2}=\\frac{y-3}{1}=\\frac{z}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,2,1⟩.$ From the canonical equation, we find that the line is parallel to the vector $⟨-2,1,5⟩.$ So, the normal vector of the plane is \n\n$$\nn=⟨-2,1,5⟩.\n$$\n\nUsing the dot product, we can find the equation of the plane as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,5⟩ & =⟨0,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,1,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,5⟩ & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to obtain the Cartesian equation of the plane, we substitute $r=⟨x,y,z⟩$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,1,5⟩ & =7 \\\\ -2x+y+5z & =7 \\\\ -2x+y+5z-7 & =0 \\\\ 2x-y-5z+7 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3d11e9af-f90d-5fbe-a96b-a527fdd70135" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423963}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423963 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423960 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13bd6234-56f6-541c-bfc5-f390a8cb5bfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423950} {:answer/id #uuid "1d1ce09d-4b43-5ecf-b718-dbc33ca70dc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,2,3⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423951} {:answer/id #uuid "2c57426d-3447-5790-bc09-7f27391e4e89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,3⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-2,3⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423952} {:answer/id #uuid "95f99c20-a235-5660-8d6b-b04b727483d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-2,3⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423955} {:answer/id #uuid "b1292071-77e9-579a-8b2f-0a1e4da37f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(r-⟨0,0,\\frac{1}{3}⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-2,3⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423957}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423955} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fa9de33-9d04-55cd-94a1-cecb483c4e8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423959}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e005b4ab-002a-57d1-b9b7-3fc85eeb395f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70819" :question/problem "Given the Cartesian equation $x-2y+3z=0$ of the plane $Π$, find an equation of $Π$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $Π$ is $n=⟨1,-2,3⟩.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $Π$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2y+3z & =0 \\\\ 3z & =-x+2y \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{2}{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=0.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,0)$ lies on $Π.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨0,0,0⟩.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-⟨0,0,0⟩)\\cdot ⟨1,-2,3⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "eee37068-88fb-59e1-930d-db5693058840" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423961}}] :activity/title "The Cartesian Equation of a Plane" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423948}]}
